#
# The Wi-Fi survey with a USB stick: 6 starts the pretend listen, networks
# and a look-alike come in, the chart catches a kick-off attack, and 5 goes
# back to the findings.
#
# The made-up data sets have no USB stick, so this clip runs on a made-up
# test folder with a free one, built by survey.setup (scripts/demo-gifs.sh
# does that by itself). The clock in the title bar is the computer's own.
1000 --page survey --data live
# 6 starts the pretend listen; --settle-ms is the time after each key, so
# the listen has run for (keys x settle) when the picture is taken.
400 --page survey --data live --keys 6 --settle-ms 300
300 --page survey --data live --keys 6 --settle-ms {1..6}000
# 5 swaps to the chart (twice the settle): channel 6 busy, then at 21 s a
# kick-off attack turns channel 11 red.
300 --page survey --data live --keys 6,5 --settle-ms 5000
300 --page survey --data live --keys 6,5 --settle-ms 7500
300 --page survey --data live --keys 6,5 --settle-ms 10000
1300 --page survey --data live --keys 6,5 --settle-ms 10500
# 5 again goes back to the list, findings first (22.5 s).
2000 --page survey --data live --keys 6,5,5 --settle-ms 7500
